{"book":23,"chapter":16,"context":{"chapter":16,"title":"Moab's Pride, Moab's Tears","summary":"Moab's refugees are urged to send tribute to Zion and seek shelter there, where a throne of mercy will stand in David's tent. But Moab's pride brings ruin, the prophet weeps over its vineyards, and within three years its glory will fade.","background":"Verse 1 recalls that Moab once paid Israel tribute in lambs and wool (2 Kings 3:4). The vineyards of Sibmah and Heshbon were famous; their branches spreading 'over the sea' (v. 8) picture a far-reaching vine. Jeremiah 48 reuses much of this oracle.","customs":[{"term":"The years of an hireling","verses":"16:14","note":"A hired worker's term was counted exactly. 'Three years' means precisely that, and no more."}],"watchFor":["A throne 'established in mercy… in the tabernacle of David' (v. 5).","The prophet's inner parts 'sound like an harp' for Moab (v. 11).","Moab prays at its high place, but in vain (v. 12)."],"connections":["2 Kings 3:4","Jeremiah 48:29-36","Amos 9:11","Ruth 1:4"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["שִׁלְחוּ","shilchu-","H7971","HVqv2mp","send"],["כַר","khar","H3733","HNcmsa","a lamb"],["מֹשֵׁל","moshel-","H4910","HVqrmsc","[the] ruler of"],["אֶרֶץ","'eretz","H776","HNcfsa","[the] land"],["מִסֶּלַע","misela'","H5554","HR/Npl","from Sela"],["מִדְבָּרָה","midbarah","H4057","HNcmsa/Sd","[the] wilderness towards"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["הַר","har","H2022","HNcmsc","[the] mountain of"],["בַּת","bat-","H1323","HNcfsc","[the] daughter of"],["צִיּוֹן","tziyon","H6726","HNpl","Zion"]],"x":[[12003004,12003004,6],[23010032,23010032,6],[12014007,12014007,5],[10008002,10008002,3]],"xn":4},"2":{"w":[["וְהָיָה","vehayah","H1961","Hc/Vqq3ms","and it will be"],["כְעוֹף","khe'of-","H5775","HR/Ncmsa","like a bird"],["נוֹדֵד","noded","H5074","HVqrmsa","fluttering"],["קֵן","ken","H7064","HNcmsa","a nest"],["מְשֻׁלָּח","meshulach","H7971","HVPsmsa","sent away"],["תִּהְיֶינָה","tihyeinah","H1961","HVqi3fp","they will be"],["בְּנו